Negative control for the forced affordance's colour family (`H2`).

Repaints both halves — the frame's ring and the chip — in the warning family and
changes nothing else: same outline technique, same standoff, same geometry
(`R6-18`), same armed-only condition. So the only claim that can go red is the
ruled one: a forced page is a mode the developer CHOSE, dressed in the primary
family, never in the family a page reports trouble in.

Re-targeted 2026-08-13 after the `R7-7`/`R7-5` changes moved both hunks' context
(the ring gained its standoff, the chip gained a header row). Same claim, same
red, current source.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the chosen-mode colour case — every class the affordance draws itself with
resolves to primary or secondary, and none to warning, danger or success.

